From 06ca63e5b1837127de5660a20191aea56913a8bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Bernauer <sebastian.bernauer@stackable.tech>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:57:22 +0100
Subject: Fall back to the managed warehouse in the Iceberg REST catalog

Creating a namespace through the HMS-embedded Iceberg REST catalog fails with

    Warehouse location is not set: hive.metastore.warehouse.external.dir=null

when only hive.metastore.warehouse.dir is configured. Hive's copy of the Iceberg HiveCatalog
requires the external warehouse to be set, while HMS itself (Warehouse#getWhRootExternal) falls
back to hive.metastore.warehouse.dir. This patch adds the same fallback to HiveCatalog, so
namespaces created through the REST catalog get the same location as databases created through
Thrift.

It also backports the HiveCatalog#initialize part of HIVE-29461 (fixed in Hive 4.3.0): the
external-warehouse catalog property, which HMSCatalogFactory already passes, is now applied. This
makes the metastore.warehouse.external.dir spelling work as well. HMSCatalogFactory now only passes
the property when it is non-empty, as MetastoreConf defaults it to "" and initialize would reject
that.

The fallback is not fixed upstream yet, Hive master still requires the external warehouse.
